+/*!
+   \fn double QCborStreamReader::toNumber() const
+   \since 6.13
+
+   Returns the value of the current element as a \c double, whichever CBOR
+   numeric type it was encoded as: unsigned or negative integer, or half-,
+   single- or double-precision floating point. Floating-point values,
+   including infinities and NaNs, are converted without loss. Integers whose
+   magnitude exceeds 2\sup{53} may not be exactly representable as a
+   \c double; they are rounded to the nearest representable value. This
+   covers the full range of CBOR integers, from -2\sup{64} to
+   2\sup{64} - 1.
+
+   This function does not perform any type conversions from non-numeric types,
+   including from boolean, string or CBOR tag (such as a big number or decimal
+   fraction). Therefore, it may only be called if isNumber() is true; calling
+   it in any other condition is an error.
